        "essence_text": "A claustrophobic, real-time study of a family and a justice system trying to understand an unthinkable accusation. Single-take episodes lock you inside rooms where every glance, silence, and outburst lands with documentary force. The series is less a whodunit than a how-did-we-get-here, tracing online culture, boyhood, and parental blind spots without easy answers. Performances feel lived-in and raw, turning procedural beats into emotional endurance. It leaves a lingering unease about what we fail to see in children until it is too late."
